WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.810
About 500 people live in Shishmaref, on
a barrier island near the Bering Strait.

2
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.290
The island is only about
a quarter of a mile wide.

3
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.210
Its residents voted to
relocate in 1973, in 2002,

4
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.610
and again in 2016.

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.110
Yet the village is still there.

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.950
Why vote to move, and why stay?

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.930
Do families prefer the city?

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.500
Does a new oil field need the land?

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.970
In this mission, you'll measure how
fast extreme environments are changing,

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.690
from the Arctic to hot drylands.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.110
Then you'll weigh how people adapt, from
harvesting rainwater to better flood

12
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.330
warnings.

13
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.250
Your mission: explain why
Shishmaref has voted to move,

14
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.830
and why it is still there.
